   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the highway law, in relation to the designation of a portion of the state highway system to be known as the \"Charles Varese Memorial Highway\"",
    "basePrintNo": "S6705",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6705-2009",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Add §343-x, Hway L",
    "lawSection": "Highway Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S6705\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\nAn act to amend the highway law, in relation to the designation of a\nportion of the state highway system to be known as the \"Charles Varese\nMemorial Highway\"\n\n\n SUMMARY :\nThis bill would add a new section, 343-x, to the highway law.  The\nsection would designate the section of state route 25A in the village\nof Northport, within the town of Huntington, county of Suffolk, shall\nbe known as the \"Charles Varese Memorial Highway\". The bill also\ndirects the commissioner of transportation to provide for the\ninstallation and maintenance of adequate signing of the state highway,\nhowever the designation shall be one of a ceremonial nature and the\nofficial name of such highway shall not be changed as a result.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\nOn April 15 of 2008 Charles Varese was killed on his way to the\nNorthport Firehouse, where he bravely served his community as a\nvolunteer firefighter. It is our duty to honor and memorialize those\nindividuals who exemplify the highest of admirable qualities in men so\nthat we may continue striving for greatness. Charles Varese's selfless\nacts in his service as a firefighter and community role model are a\ntestament to his character. Men like Charles Varese are few and far\nbetween, and as such must be acknowledged and honored in both life and\ndeath.\n\n FISCAL IMPACT :\nNegligible.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
